  "decision_needed": [],
  "notes": "Waiver filing: Exhibit A all-funds cash receipts and disbursements (10/1/21-9/30/22). The trim holds two versions of pages 1, 1a and the schedules page: pp2, 4, 8 are crossed out (void; pp2/4 have blank lines 26-28, p8 a blank investment schedule) and the unmarked pp1, 3, 7 are used; pp5, 6 (pages 2 and 2a) appear once. Governmental = General, Street, Cemetery, Perpetual Care, Recreation, Sales Tax (page 1); page 1a columns Surcharge, Cub Creek, Water, Sewer, Solid Waste are business-type (Surcharge spending printed on the Water line; Cub Creek kept with the utility columns as in FY2023/FY2024). Mixed rows (Local Receipts: Other, Other Capital Outlay, transfers) split by fund type; business-type statement lines from the page 1a/2a Total columns. Capital outlay functions from the Street Fund column (Streets/Highways) and the Water/Sewer columns (Utilities). Balances include investments (line 3 / line 24); line 2 beginning investments blank. Gross transfers 170,131: in Street 112,000, Cemetery 5,131, Recreation 10,000, Water 38,000, Sewer 5,000; out General 101,000, Perpetual Care 131, Sales Tax 69,000 (all line 50/20); agrees with the Schedule of Interfund Transfers (p7). Business-type receipts total 198,392 includes transfers in 43,000 (= transfers_net; no business transfers out). Schedule of investments (p7) total 172,901 agrees with line 27. No outstanding debt listed although Street Fund paid Debt Service 88,271. County treasurer balances 10/1/21 1,823.00 and 9/30/22 4,237.00 are not in the totals. Detail is one line per Exhibit A fund column. No balance-sheet statement other than lines 25-28. Read pages 1-8 of 8."
